  "helpQ1": "Does noor need the internet?",
  "helpA1": "No. Everything works offline. The only exception is optional Quran audio downloads, which start only when you tap a download icon.",
  "helpQ2": "Where does my data go?",
  "helpA2": "Nowhere. Your ticked prayers, bookmarks, settings and location stay on your phone in an encrypted database. There are no ads and no tracking.",
  "helpQ3": "Why did the adhan not sound?",
  "helpA3": "Check that notifications are allowed for noor, that \"Alarms & reminders\" is allowed, that battery optimisation is off for noor, and that the phone is not in Do Not Disturb. Settings has a test button for the adhan.",
  "helpQ4": "How are prayer times calculated?",
  "helpA4": "On your phone, from your location, using the calculation method and madhab chosen in Settings. You can change them there at any time.",
  "helpQ5": "Why does noor ask for location?",
  "helpA5": "Only to work out prayer times for where you are. It is used on your phone and never sent anywhere. If location is off, noor uses a default location and tells you so.",
  "helpQ6": "How do I back up my data?",
  "helpA6": "Open Settings, then Backup & Restore. It creates an encrypted file that you keep. Only you know the passphrase, so keep it safe.",
  "helpQ7": "How is the progress percentage worked out?",
  "helpA7": "It is the prayers you ticked in the last 7 days divided by the prayers possible (5 per day), counting only days since your first tick. Tap the ? on the progress card for details.",
  "helpQ8": "How do I change the theme?",
  "helpA8": "Open Settings, then Display, and choose Nebula, Dawn, Mushaf or Emerald Night, or follow the system setting.",
  "helpQ9": "How do I report a problem?",
  "helpA9": "Open Settings, then Send Feedback. Describe what happened and what you expected.",
